feat(sysauth): render LuCI auth plugin fields on the login page

luci-base hands the login template four scope variables for auth plugins
- auth_fields, auth_message, auth_html and auth_assets - and picks the
theme's own sysauth template over its generic one whenever the theme
ships one (dispatcher.uc). This theme ships one and references none of
them, so on Argon a plugin's extra fields, its notice, its markup and
its script are all dropped and the user only ever sees username and
password. The in-tree themes (bootstrap, footstrap) render all four.

The mechanism landed in luci-base after this theme's templates were
rewritten into ucode, which is why the gap went unnoticed.

Render the four in Argon's own markup: plugin fields join the existing
.input-container so they inherit its input styling, the message reuses
.errorbox, and the asset scripts are emitted last so a plugin's markup
is in the document before its script runs. No stylesheet change, so the
compiled CSS does not need regenerating.

The credentials alert is gated on !auth_plugin and the plugin message is
shown beside it rather than instead of it. auth_plugin is set only on
the render that follows an accepted password, so the two alerts now
distinguish a wrong password from a password that was right with a
challenge still pending, instead of one hiding the other.

--- a/ucode/template/themes/argon/sysauth.ut
+++ b/ucode/template/themes/argon/sysauth.ut
@@ -129,10 +129,22 @@
 			<!-- Login Form Start -->
 			<form class="form-login" method="post" action="{{ http.getenv("REQUEST_URI") }}">
 
-				{%- if (fuser): %}
+				{#-
+				 `auth_plugin` is set only on the render that follows an ACCEPTED password
+				 (dispatcher.uc), so it is what separates "the password was wrong" from "the
+				 password was right and a plugin wants more". Gating the credentials alert on
+				 `!auth_plugin` and showing `auth_message` beside it rather than instead of it
+				 covers all four states: a wrong password, a wrong password with a challenge
+				 already pending, the challenge prompt itself, and a failed challenge.
+				-#}
+				{%- if (fuser && !auth_plugin): %}
 				<div class="errorbox">{{ _('Invalid username and/or password! Please try again.') }}</div>
 				{% endif -%}
 
+				{%- if (auth_message): %}
+				<div class="errorbox">{{ auth_message }}</div>
+				{% endif -%}
+
 				<div class="input-container">
 					<div class="input-group user-icon">
 						<input class="cbi-input-user" id="cbi-input-user" type="text" name="luci_username" value="{{ entityencode(duser, true) }}" />
@@ -142,10 +154,39 @@
